    "site_desc": "Mature spruce-moss stand on a valley floor some 270 m above mean sea level, surrounded by plateaus some 200 m higher. The site is close to the Romaine-2 hydroelectric reservoir and was first instrumented in 2018 as part of a research project with Hydro-Québec, a state-owned company responsible for the distribution and production of electricity in Quebec, eastern Canada. The site was affected by the passage of the spruce budworm before 2018 (but at an unknown date).",
